======= B3_RefusedStructField.sol =======
{"absolutePath":"B3_RefusedStructField.sol","exportedSymbols":{"B3_RefusedStructField":[109]},"id":110,"license":"MIT","nodeType":"SourceUnit","nodes":[{"id":1,"literals":["solidity","^","0.8",".20"],"nodeType":"PragmaDirective","src":"32:24:0"},{"abstract":false,"baseContracts":[],"canonicalName":"B3_RefusedStructField","contractDependencies":[],"contractKind":"contract","documentation":{"id":2,"nodeType":"StructuredDocumentation","src":"58:2869:0","text":"ISOLATES candidate 2 of the farming/deposit coords-gate: branching on a\n SCALAR FIELD of a struct that also contains a mapping, i.e. a field the\n coordinate classifier REFUSES because of the shape of its container.\n WHERE IT COMES FROM. FarmingPool holds `FarmingLib.Data private _farm`,\n whose two members are FarmAccounting.Info (four scalars) and\n UserAccounting.Info (two scalars plus `mapping(address => int256)\n corrections`). deposit reaches\n     if (duration > 0) { ... }                 // FarmAccounting, uint32\n     if (block.timestamp != checkpoint) { ... } // UserAccounting, uint40\n and BOTH live inside `_farm`. On the deposit arms `state._farm` is REFUSED\n as a coordinate, so neither field constrains the region and neither shows up\n in the payload the shrink loop compares.\n WHY D02_StructWithMapping DOES NOT COVER THIS. D02 declares the shape but\n its only unit, `setFeeReceiver`, never reads a struct field -- it was built\n to reproduce a z3 `datatype is not well-founded` error, and it branches on\n `msg.sender == owner`. Nothing there asks whether a scalar field of such a\n struct can be a coordinate.\n EXPECTED, `probe`: the driver prints `state.d.duration` (or the whole\n `state.d`) among its REFUSED coordinates, and the two paths' counterexamples\n then agree on `amount` and `msg.sender` -- the coordinate gate.\n \u26d4 HOW TO RUN IT, and the first attempt got this wrong. Under `--focus\n --max-tx 1` NOTHING CAN WRITE `d.duration`: the dispatcher is restricted to\n the unit itself, so the field keeps its zero-value at entry, only the `else`\n side of `d.duration > 0` is reachable, and the driver witnesses TWO paths\n where ctrlParam witnesses three. With no sibling to separate from, the one\n live path certifies trivially -- and reading that as \"the refused field is\n harmless\" would be reading a run in which the discriminating object was\n never built. The measured tell is the path count, not the verdict:\n     ctrlParam  3 witnessed paths   1 certified / 2 not\n     ctrlPlain  2 witnessed paths   1 certified / 1 not\n     probe      2 witnessed paths   1 certified / 1 not\n so ctrlPlain and probe are not comparable to ctrlParam either.\n REQUIRED: `--scope setDuration,probe --max-tx 2`, which is the only shape\n that buys a witness for state a different function has to write.\n TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS, because two different things could be responsible:\n   * `ctrlPlain` branches on a scalar state variable of the same type that is\n     NOT inside any struct. If this one also gets refused, the mapping in the\n     container is not what matters -- the type is.\n   * `ctrlParam` branches on the parameter. It must certify; if it does not,\n     the run measured the harness rather than the candidate."},"fullyImplemented":true,"id":109,"linearizedBaseContracts":[109],"name":"B3_RefusedStructField","nameLocation":"2936:21:0","nodeType":"ContractDefinition","nodes":[{"canonicalName":"B3_RefusedStructField.D","id":9,"members":[{"constant":false,"id":4,"mutability":"mutable","name":"duration","nameLocation":"2990:8:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":9,"src":"2983:15:0","stateVariable":false,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"},"typeName":{"id":3,"name":"uint32","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"2983:6:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"visibility":"internal"},{"constant":false,"id":8,"mutability":"mutable","name":"corrections","nameLocation":"3035:11:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":9,"src":"3008:38:0","stateVariable":false,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_mapping$_t_address_$_t_int256_$","typeString":"mapping(address => int256)"},"typeName":{"id":7,"keyName":"","keyNameLocation":"-1:-1:-1","keyType":{"id":5,"name":"address","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"3016:7:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_address","typeString":"address"}},"nodeType":"Mapping","src":"3008:26:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_mapping$_t_address_$_t_int256_$","typeString":"mapping(address => int256)"},"valueName":"","valueNameLocation":"-1:-1:-1","valueType":{"id":6,"name":"int256","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"3027:6:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_int256","typeString":"int256"}}},"visibility":"internal"}],"name":"D","nameLocation":"2971:1:0","nodeType":"StructDefinition","scope":109,"src":"2964:89:0","visibility":"public"},{"constant":false,"id":12,"mutability":"mutable","name":"d","nameLocation":"3070:1:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":109,"src":"3059:12:0","stateVariable":true,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_struct$_D_$9_storage","typeString":"struct B3_RefusedStructField.D"},"typeName":{"id":11,"nodeType":"UserDefinedTypeName","pathNode":{"id":10,"name":"D","nameLocations":["3059:1:0"],"nodeType":"IdentifierPath","referencedDeclaration":9,"src":"3059:1:0"},"referencedDeclaration":9,"src":"3059:1:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_struct$_D_$9_storage_ptr","typeString":"struct B3_RefusedStructField.D"}},"visibility":"internal"},{"constant":false,"functionSelector":"b02a0400","id":14,"mutability":"mutable","name":"plainDuration","nameLocation":"3091:13:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":109,"src":"3077:27:0","stateVariable":true,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"},"typeName":{"id":13,"name":"uint32","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"3077:6:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"visibility":"public"},{"constant":false,"functionSelector":"51f91066","id":16,"mutability":"mutable","name":"tag","nameLocation":"3125:3:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":109,"src":"3110:18:0","stateVariable":true,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"},"typeName":{"id":15,"name":"uint256","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"3110:7:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"}},"visibility":"public"},{"body":{"id":34,"nodeType":"Block","src":"3796:58:0","statements":[{"expression":{"id":28,"isConstant":false,"isLValue":false,"isPure":false,"lValueRequested":false,"leftHandSide":{"expression":{"id":24,"name":"d","nodeType":"Identifier","overloadedDeclarations":[],"referencedDeclaration":12,"src":"3806:1:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_struct$_D_$9_storage","typeString":"struct B3_RefusedStructField.D storage ref"}},"id":26,"isConstant":false,"isLValue":true,"isPure":false,"lValueRequested":true,"memberLocation":"3808:8:0","memberName":"duration","nodeType":"MemberAccess","referencedDeclaration":4,"src":"3806:10:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"nodeType":"Assignment","operator":"=","rightHandSide":{"id":27,"name":"v","nodeType":"Identifier","overloadedDeclarations":[],"referencedDeclaration":19,"src":"3819:1:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"src":"3806:14:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"id":29,"nodeType":"ExpressionStatement","src":"3806:14:0"},{"expression":{"id":32,"isConstant":false,"isLValue":false,"isPure":false,"lValueRequested":false,"leftHandSide":{"id":30,"name":"plainDuration","nodeType":"Identifier","overloadedDeclarations":[],"referencedDeclaration":14,"src":"3830:13:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"nodeType":"Assignment","operator":"=","rightHandSide":{"id":31,"name":"w","nodeType":"Identifier","overloadedDeclarations":[],"referencedDeclaration":21,"src":"3846:1:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"src":"3830:17:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"id":33,"nodeType":"ExpressionStatement","src":"3830:17:0"}]},"documentation":{"id":17,"nodeType":"StructuredDocumentation","src":"3135:606:0","text":"\u26d4 THE FIRST VERSION TOOK ONE PARAMETER AND WROTE BOTH FIELDS FROM IT:\n     function setDuration(uint32 v) { d.duration = v; plainDuration = v; }\n Under that setter the REFUSED field is exactly recoverable from a FREE\n coordinate, so `probe` certified with regions IDENTICAL, value for\n value, to `ctrlPlain`'s -- and reading that as \"the refusal is harmless\"\n would be reading a discriminator whose two outcomes were made equal by\n construction. The two fields are now written from INDEPENDENT\n parameters, so no free coordinate determines d.duration."},"functionSelector":"e9194ec0","id":35,"implemented":true,"kind":"function","modifiers":[],"name":"setDuration","nameLocation":"3755:11:0","nodeType":"FunctionDefinition","parameters":{"id":22,"nodeType":"ParameterList","parameters":[{"constant":false,"id":19,"mutability":"mutable","name":"v","nameLocation":"3774:1:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":35,"src":"3767:8:0","stateVariable":false,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"},"typeName":{"id":18,"name":"uint32","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"3767:6:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint32","typeString":"uint32"}},"visibility":"internal"},{"constant":false,"id":21,"mutability":"mutable","name":"w","nameLocation":"3784:1:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":35,"src":"3777:8:0","stateVariable":false,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"